# Build context hygiene for deploy/content.Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs whole directories (.agents/, cluster/), so
# anything that lands inside them ships to every cluster that mounts the
# image. Two categories must not:
#
#   1. Local run state. `.agents/sessions/` accumulates a JSON transcript
#      per local `core-agent -c .agents/config.json` invocation. Baking
#      those into the content image leaks local conversation history into
#      a cluster artifact and makes the image non-reproducible (a rebuild
#      after a test run differs from one before it).
#   2. Anything the daemon never reads — the operator scripts, deploy/,
#      docs, the Go test. Excluded to keep the context small and the
#      image honest about what the agent can actually see.
#
# scripts/build-content-image.sh normally stages a minimal context under
# /tmp and copies THIS FILE next to it, because Docker reads
# .dockerignore from the context root and the root is the staging dir,
# not this directory. The rules below therefore have to hold for both
# that staged context and a naive `docker build -f
# deploy/content.Dockerfile .` from here. Category 2 only matters for the
# second case; category 1 matters for both.
#
# Keep category 1 in sync with the prune-and-assert block in
# build-content-image.sh, which enforces the same list on disk where it
# is actually checkable.

# ── 1. Local run state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.agents/sessions/
.agents/plans/*
!.agents/plans/.gitkeep
.agents/config.hub.local.json
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# ── 2. Not part of the agent's content ───────────────────────────────
deploy/
docs/
scripts/
recipe_test.go
README.md
DEMO.md

# Belt and braces. gen-tokens.sh writes live bearer tokens under
# RIG_STATE_DIR (outside this tree) precisely so they can never be here
# — these two lines cost nothing and cover the case where someone
# reintroduces the old in-tree behavior.
demo-tokens.env
users.json

.git/
.gitignore
